## Question

Can a stateless Index Sitter supervise Zotero's native extraction and indexing,
distinguish long-running work from a stall, and avoid blocking short jobs?
Also verify extraction-date provenance in real structured-text caches.

## Evidence

Report: `verification/INDEX-SITTER-LIVE.md`.
Raw observations: `bench/results/index-sitter-2026-09-05/`.
Reproduction: `verification/probes/index_sitter_live.py`.

This is a live probe, not implementation of the sitter or a change to the
requirements. Source documents and global indexing preferences stay untouched.
